<!doctype html>
<html class="no-js" lang="{{ request.locale.iso_code }}">
  <head>
    <meta charset="utf-8">
    {%- comment -%}
      Reveal safety (INF-0). theme.css hides reveal start states ([data-cv-reveal],
      [data-cm-reveal], [data-halo-reveal], .cv-split words, .cv-callout) only under
      html.js, so without JavaScript every node is visible. html.cv-reveal-timeout
      switches those start states off again: it is set when a reveal engine
      (cv-motion.js, theme.js) has not booted once the deferred scripts have run,
      or 2.5 s after the rest of the page starts to arrive, whichever comes
      first; by cv-motion.js if its boot throws; and by halo.js's onerror below.
      The 2.5 s countdown is started by the one-line script right below Shopify's
      header tag, not here: on a streamed page this part runs while the sections
      are still rendering on the server, seconds before the scripts can boot.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      (function (d, w) {
        var h = d.documentElement;
        h.className = h.className.replace('no-js', 'js');
        w.cvRevealCheck = function () {
          var ok = w.CVMotion && w.CVMotion.ready && w.CASIFY_FNS && w.CASIFY_FNS.revealReady;
          if (!ok) h.classList.add('cv-reveal-timeout');
        };
        d.addEventListener('DOMContentLoaded', function () { w.setTimeout(w.cvRevealCheck, 0); });
      })(document, window);
    </script>
    {%- comment -%}
      Shared 3D helpers for the section modules (assets/cv-*.js), before any
      stylesheet so the parser runs this at once.
      CV_THREE_URL: three.js 0.186.0, the version the modules used to import
      from cdn.jsdelivr.net, as jsDelivr's minified build in this theme's
      assets. Same server as the page, so no extra connection, and about half
      the bytes. three.module.min.js imports ./three.core.min.js by a path
      with no ?v=, so an upgrade must ship both files under new names.
      cvWebGL(): one WebGL probe per page, cached. Each module used to probe
      with a throwaway context of its own; one costs about as much as a real
      one, and Android Chrome keeps at most 8 live contexts per page.
      cvNear(el, screens): resolves once el is within that many screen
      heights of the viewport, so a section far down the page builds its 3D
      scene as the shopper scrolls towards it, not during page load.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>
      window.CV_THREE_URL = {{ 'three.module.min.js' | asset_url | json }};
      (function (w, d) {
        var gl;
        w.cvWebGL = function () {
          if (gl === undefined) {
            gl = false;
            try {
              var c = d.createElement('canvas');
              var ctx = w.WebGLRenderingContext && (c.getContext('webgl2') || c.getContext('webgl'));
              if (ctx) {
                gl = true;
                var lose = ctx.getExtension('WEBGL_lose_context');
                if (lose) lose.loseContext();
              }
            } catch (e) { gl = false; }
          }
          return gl;
        };
        w.cvNear = function (el, screens) {
          return new Promise(function (resolve) {
            if (!el || !('IntersectionObserver' in w)) { resolve(); return; }
            var io = new IntersectionObserver(function (entries) {
              for (var i = 0; i < entries.length; i++) {
                if (entries[i].isIntersecting) { io.disconnect(); resolve(); return; }
              }
            }, { rootMargin: Math.round((screens || 2) * 100) + '% 0px' });
            io.observe(el);
          });
        };
      })(window, document);
    </script>
    <meta name="viewport" content="width=device-width,initial-scale=1">
    <link rel="canonical" href="{{ canonical_url }}">
    {%- comment -%}
      The shop name is appended once. Shopify's page_title on the home page is
      the shop name itself unless the merchant sets a homepage title in Online
      Store > Preferences; it used to render "Casify | Casify". Without that
      setting the home page gets a descriptive fallback instead of a bare name.
      Product pages with no SEO title of their own (product admin > Search
      engine listing, metafield global.title_tag) build the title from the
      product title. Shopify's page_title cuts it at 70 characters, which left
      "Samsung | | Casify", cut words ("| Tough Cas") and one title for a
      design's Clear, Magnetic and Tough cases. The rule keeps the part before
      the first " | " without the device list after "Phone Case for ", and
      the last part without "Impact-Resistant", "Impact" and "Compatible":
      "Stay Cozy Patchwork Bunny Christmas Phone Case | Clear Case | Casify".
      Over 70 characters it tries, in order: "Case" off the case type,
      "Christmas" off the name, then both. Words are never cut. The result is
      escaped like page_title, so the escape on og:title leaves it as it is.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign seo_title = page_title | default: shop.name
      if template.name == 'index' and seo_title == shop.name
        assign seo_title = 'general.meta.home_title' | t: shop: shop.name
      elsif template.name == 'product' and product.metafields.global.title_tag == blank
        assign title_parts = product.title | split: ' | '
        assign title_name = title_parts.first | default: product.title
        if title_name contains 'Phone Case for '
          assign title_name = title_name | split: 'Phone Case for ' | first | append: 'Phone Case'
        endif
        assign title_kind = ''
        if title_parts.size > 1
          assign title_kind = title_parts.last | remove: ' Impact-Resistant' | remove: ' Impact' | remove: ' Compatible' | prepend: ' | '
        endif
        assign title_kind_short = title_kind
        assign title_kind_end = title_kind | slice: -5, 5
        if title_kind_end == ' Case'
          assign title_kind_size = title_kind.size | minus: 5
          assign title_kind_short = title_kind | slice: 0, title_kind_size
        endif
        assign title_name_short = title_name | replace: ' Christmas Phone Case', ' Phone Case'
        assign title_shop = ' | ' | append: shop.name
        if product.title contains shop.name
          assign title_shop = ''
        endif
        assign seo_title = title_name | append: title_kind | append: title_shop
        if seo_title.size > 70
          assign seo_title = title_name | append: title_kind_short | append: title_shop
        endif
        if seo_title.size > 70
          assign seo_title = title_name_short | append: title_kind | append: title_shop
        endif
        if seo_title.size > 70
          assign seo_title = title_name_short | append: title_kind_short | append: title_shop
        endif
        assign seo_title = seo_title | escape
      else
        if current_tags
          assign joined_tags = current_tags | join: ', '
          assign tagged_label = 'general.meta.tagged' | t: tags: joined_tags
          assign seo_title = seo_title | append: ', ' | append: tagged_label
        endif
        if current_page != 1
          assign page_label = 'general.meta.page' | t: page: current_page
          assign seo_title = seo_title | append: ', ' | append: page_label
        endif
        unless seo_title contains shop.name
          assign seo_title = seo_title | append: ' | ' | append: shop.name
        endunless
      endif
    -%}
    <title>{{ seo_title }}</title>
    {%- comment -%}
      page_description is the merchant's own SEO text (Online Store >
      Preferences for the home page, or the product, collection or page's own
      description). When it is empty, fall back to a line built only from
      confirmed store facts. Cart and search stay without one: they aren't indexed.
      Product pages with no SEO description of their own (metafield
      global.description_tag) take theirs from
      snippets/cv-product-meta-description.liquid instead of Shopify's text;
      the snippet's comment has the rule. It returns plain text, escaped below.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign meta_description = page_description
      if template.name == 'product' and product.metafields.global.description_tag == blank
        capture product_meta_description
          render 'cv-product-meta-description', product: product
        endcapture
        if product_meta_description != blank
          assign meta_description = product_meta_description
        endif
      endif
      if meta_description == blank
        case template.name
          when 'index'
            assign meta_description = 'general.meta.home_description' | t: shop: shop.name
          when 'product'
            assign meta_description = 'general.meta.product_description' | t: title: product.title, shop: shop.name
          when 'collection', 'list-collections', 'page', 'blog', 'article'
            assign meta_description = 'general.meta.listing_description' | t: title: page_title, shop: shop.name
        endcase
      endif
    -%}
    {%- if meta_description != blank -%}<meta name="description" content="{{ meta_description | escape }}">{%- endif -%}
    {%- if settings.favicon != blank -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 48, height: 48 }}">
      <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ settings.favicon | image_url: width: 180, height: 180 }}">
    {%- else -%}
      <link rel="icon" type="image/png" href="{{ 'casify-logo-mark.png' | asset_url }}">
      <link rel="apple-touch-icon" href="{{ 'casify-logo-mark.png' | asset_url }}">
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%}
      Social share preview. product.metafields.custom.og_image is a real,
      per-product branded 1200x630 card (real product photo + real name/price)
      set via the Admin API — never fabricated data. Everywhere else Shopify's
      page_image is used: the product, collection or article image, or on the
      home page the social sharing image from Online Store > Preferences.
      image_url returns protocol-relative URLs, so https: is prefixed —
      crawlers need absolute og:image URLs.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign og_image = product.metafields.custom.og_image.value
      assign og_image_width = 1200
      assign og_image_height = 630
      if og_image == blank and page_image != blank
        assign og_image = page_image | image_url: width: 1200 | prepend: 'https:'
        assign og_image_width = page_image.width | at_most: 1200
        assign og_image_height = page_image.height | times: og_image_width | divided_by: page_image.width
      endif
      assign og_title = seo_title
      assign og_description = meta_description | default: shop.description
    -%}
    <meta property="og:site_name" content="{{ shop.name | escape }}">
    <meta property="og:title" content="{{ og_title | escape }}">
    {%- if og_description != blank -%}<meta property="og:description" content="{{ og_description | escape }}">{%- endif -%}
    <meta property="og:url" content="{{ canonical_url }}">
    <meta property="og:type" content="{% if template.name == 'product' %}product{% else %}website{% endif %}">
    {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
      <meta property="og:price:amount" content="{{ product.price | money_without_currency | strip_html | escape }}">
      <meta property="og:price:currency" content="{{ cart.currency.iso_code }}">
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if og_image != blank -%}
      <meta property="og:image" content="{{ og_image }}">
      <meta property="og:image:width" content="{{ og_image_width }}">
      <meta property="og:image:height" content="{{ og_image_height }}">
      <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary_large_image">
      <meta name="twitter:image" content="{{ og_image }}">
    {%- else -%}
      <meta name="twitter:card" content="summary">
    {%- endif -%}
    <meta name="twitter:title" content="{{ og_title | escape }}">
    {%- if og_description != blank -%}<meta name="twitter:description" content="{{ og_description | escape }}">{%- endif -%}
    {%- if template.name == 'index' -%}
      {%- comment -%} Organization + WebSite structured data. The search URL template is assigned in the liquid block: a literal brace inside an output tag breaks Liquid's tokenizer. {%- endcomment -%}
      {%- liquid
        if settings.logo != blank
          assign org_logo = settings.logo | image_url: width: 600 | prepend: 'https:'
        else
          assign org_logo = 'casify-logo-mark.png' | asset_url | prepend: 'https:'
        endif
        assign org_same_as = ''
        assign social_keys = 'social_instagram,social_tiktok,social_pinterest,social_facebook' | split: ','
        for social in social_keys
          if settings[social] != blank
            assign org_same_as = org_same_as | append: settings[social] | append: '|'
          endif
        endfor
        assign org_same_as = org_same_as | split: '|'
        assign search_template = shop.url | append: routes.search_url | append: '?q={search_term_string}'
      -%}
      <script type="application/ld+json">
        {
          "@context": "https://schema.org",
          "@graph": [
            {
              "@type": "Organization",
              "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#organization' | json }},
              "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
              "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
              "logo": {{ org_logo | json }}
              {%- if org_same_as.size > 0 -%},
              "sameAs": {{ org_same_as | json }}
              {%- endif %}
            },
            {
              "@type": "WebSite",
              "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#website' | json }},
              "name": {{ shop.name | json }},
              "url": {{ shop.url | json }},
              "publisher": { "@id": {{ shop.url | append: '/#organization' | json }} },
              "potentialAction": {
                "@type": "SearchAction",
                "target": {
                  "@type": "EntryPoint",
                  "urlTemplate": {{ search_template | json }}
                },
                "query-input": "required name=search_term_string"
              }
            }
          ]
        }
      </script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- render 'cv-fonts' -%}
    {{ 'theme.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {%- comment -%}
      Commerce motion (INF-3): fly to the bag, button morphs, drawer entrance.
      The script is deferred right after cart.js (end of body); nothing calls it
      at parse, and every other script listens for its events instead of
      requiring it.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {{ 'cv-commerce-motion.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {%- render 'palette-vars' -%}
    <script>window.themeMoneyFormat = {{ shop.money_format | json }};</script>
    {%- comment -%}
      Streaming. Shopify sends this layout in two parts. Everything above its
      header tag on the next line goes to the browser as soon as it is rendered,
      while the sections are still rendering, so the stylesheets, font rules and
      inline scripts up there load during that wait. The rest of the page
      follows when the sections are done. Rules for the part above the tag:
      - It never reads the rendered sections (no "contains" check on the page
        content). That would render every section first, and the early part
        would leave only when the whole page is ready.
      - No inline script there reads window.Shopify: the tag defines it.
      - The tag stays plain and inside head: no filter, no if or capture around
        it, not in a snippet.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {{ content_for_header }}
        {%- comment -%} Reveal safety countdown (see the top of this file): 2.5 s from the moment the rest of the page starts to arrive. {%- endcomment -%}
    <script>window.setTimeout(window.cvRevealCheck, 2500);</script>
    {%- comment -%}
      Script loading. Everything from here to the end of head reads
      content_for_layout, which is why it sits below Shopify's header tag.
      content_for_layout is fully rendered by now, so a section's own markup
      tells us whether its script is needed: each section-specific script below
      loads only when that section is on the page. In the theme editor
      (request.design_mode) everything loads, because a section added there is
      injected without re-rendering this layout.
      Generic GSAP plugin opt-ins: a section prints data-cv-gsap-drag or
      data-cv-gsap-flip anywhere in its first server render (Flip also brings
      MotionPathPlugin), so no unit edits this layout for a plugin.
    {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- liquid
      assign editor = request.design_mode
      assign shop_page = false
      if template.name == 'collection' or template.name == 'list-collections' or template.name == 'page' or template.name == 'policy'
        assign shop_page = true
      endif
      assign gsap_drag = false
      if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvtr' or content_for_layout contains 'data-cv-gsap-drag'
        assign gsap_drag = true
      endif
      assign gsap_flip = false
      if editor or shop_page or template.name == 'product' or content_for_layout contains 'data-cv-gsap-flip'
        assign gsap_flip = true
      endif
      assign gsap_path = gsap_flip
      assign gsap_text = false
      if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvsu'
        assign gsap_text = true
      endif
    -%}
    {%- comment -%} Googly eyes on Add to bag and Buy now: the product page's buttons and the quick pick's. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- assign buy_eyes = false -%}
    {%- if editor or template.name == 'product' or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvqp-open' -%}
      {%- assign buy_eyes = true -%}
      {{ 'cv-eyes.css' | asset_url | stylesheet_tag }}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%} GSAP + plugins in <head>, deferred: registered before any theme script runs, including scripts printed by sections. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- render 'gsap', drag: gsap_drag, flip: gsap_flip, path: gsap_path, text: gsap_text -%}
    {%- comment -%} Anime.js (snippets/animejs.liquid): only on pages whose markup opts in with a data-anime attribute. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-anime' -%}
      {%- render 'animejs' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%} Motion (snippets/motion.liquid): only on pages whose markup opts in with a data-motion-dev attribute. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-motion-dev' -%}
      {%- render 'motion' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
  </head>
  {%- liquid
    assign tpl_class = ''
    if template.name == 'product'
      assign tpl_class = ' cv-tpl'
    endif
  -%}
  <body class="template-{{ template.name }}{{ tpl_class }}">
    <a href="#MainContent" class="cm-skip-link">Skip to content</a>
    {% sections 'header-group' %}
    <main id="MainContent" role="main" tabindex="-1">{{ content_for_layout }}</main>
    {% sections 'footer-group' %}
    {% render 'cart-drawer' %}
    {%- comment -%} Quick pick (snippets/cv-quick-pick.liquid): one dialog per page, only when a card on the page asks for colour and phone before adding. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvqp-open' -%}
      {%- render 'cv-quick-pick', sid: 'page' -%}
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%} Header behaviour + motion. {%- endcomment -%}
    <script src="{{ 'cv-header.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    <script src="{{ 'cv-footer.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    <script src="{{ 'casify-data.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    <script src="{{ 'theme.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'halo-' -%}
      {%- comment -%} halo.js is the only engine for [data-halo-reveal]: if it fails to load, show those nodes. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'halo.js' | asset_url }}" defer onerror="document.documentElement.classList.add('cv-reveal-timeout')"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- comment -%} Shared design-system motion: every page opts in by attribute. {%- endcomment -%}
    <script src="{{ 'cv-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- comment -%} Bespoke section motion; each file also no-ops without its section's markup. {%- endcomment -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cv-proof' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "The proof" (sections/cv-social-proof.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-proof-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvsp' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Convert — Spotlight" (sections/cv-spotlight.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-spotlight-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvsh' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Showcase cards" (sections/cv-showcase.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-showcase-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvhang' -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-hanging-cards.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvoc' -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-offer-courier.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvft' -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-feature-tabs.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvcl' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Multimedia collage" (sections/cv-collage.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-collage-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if gsap_text -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Email signup banner" (sections/cv-signup-banner.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-signup-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvsr' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Scrolling reviews" (sections/cv-scrolling-reviews.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-scrolling-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvtr' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Review rail" (sections/cv-trustpilot.liquid). Gated on its own marker, not gsap_drag, so the generic drag opt-in does not ship it. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-trustpilot.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-csv' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "CS Video" theme block (blocks/cs-video.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'casify-cs-video.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvap' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Apps" (sections/cv-apps.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-apps.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvfr' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Facebook reviews" (sections/facebook-reviews.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-facebook-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvps' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "3D phone scan" (sections/cv-phone-scan.liquid): a module; it imports three.js only when WebGL works and motion is allowed. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-phone-scan.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvorbit' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "The collection, in 3D" (sections/cv-orbit.liquid): a module; it imports three.js only when WebGL works. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-orbit.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvcx' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Comparison lab" (sections/cv-compare.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-compare-lab.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvvs-row' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Us vs. them" (sections/cv-vs.liquid): module; GSAP rows + a three.js VS token. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-vs.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cv-awning' -%}
      {%- comment -%} Main-image awning (snippets/cv-awning.liquid): module; three.js canopy + GSAP unroll, gusts and the red/teal swipe. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-awning.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cv-ptag' -%}
      {%- comment -%} Price tag on the main photo (snippets/cv-photo-price.liquid): module; three.js card on a string, GSAP swing + flip. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-price-tag.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvqp-open' -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-quick-pick.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if buy_eyes -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-eyes.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvvr' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Product: video reviews" (sections/cv-pdp-video-reviews.liquid): ahead of cv-product.js so it hears the buy box's first "cvs:change". {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-video-reviews.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if template.name == 'product' -%}
      {%- comment -%} Order Slip (cv-product.liquid) and Shop Counter (cv-product-counter.liquid) share cv-product.js; each script no-ops without its markup. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-product.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pack-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-story.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-slip-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-counter.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-counter-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
      {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvc-sales' -%}
        {%- comment -%} The Shop Counter's sales notes: a module after the counter motion; it rolls the numbers up and imports three.js for the flame and rocket only when WebGL works and motion is allowed. {%- endcomment -%}
        <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-pdp-sales.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvc-promises' -%}
        {%- comment -%} The Shop Counter's promise stamps: a module after the counter motion; GSAP deals the stamps in, and three.js draws the van, the return loop and the packing box only when WebGL works and motion is allowed. {%- endcomment -%}
        <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-pdp-promises.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
      {%- endif -%}
      {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvcf' -%}
        {%- comment -%} The Shop Counter's case features: a module after the counter motion; GSAP deals the tiles in, and three.js draws a scene per tile only when WebGL works and motion is allowed. {%- endcomment -%}
        <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-case-features.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
      {%- endif -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-home-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-pdp-reviews.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
      <script src="{{ 'cv-customer-experience.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvcr' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Product: colour carousel" (sections/cv-pdp-carousel.liquid): a module placed after cv-product.js so the buy box is ready; it imports three.js only when WebGL works and motion is allowed. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script type="module" src="{{ 'cv-pdp-carousel.js' | asset_url }}"></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvdl' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Product: delivery dates" (sections/cv-pdp-delivery.liquid). {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-delivery.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-cvba' -%}
      {%- comment -%} "Product: before & after" (sections/cv-pdp-before-after.liquid): it can be added to any template, so it loads by markup rather than on product pages only. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pdp-before-after.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    {%- if shop_page -%}
      {%- comment -%} Aisle (filters, pack meter), aisles, contact letterbox, rule book; each module no-ops without its markup. {%- endcomment -%}
      <script src="{{ 'cv-pages.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
    <script src="{{ 'cart.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- comment -%} Commerce motion slot, right after cart.js (see the stylesheet slot in <head>). {%- endcomment -%}
    <script src="{{ 'cv-commerce-motion.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- if editor or content_for_layout contains 'data-build-box' -%}
      <script src="{{ 'build-box.js' | asset_url }}" defer></script>
    {%- endif -%}
  </body>
</html>
